// @run
// @log 1
// A WIDE STORE MUST FORCE THE MEMORY SECTION BY ITSELF, with no load anywhere in
// the program.
//
// The memory section is usage-gated: it is emitted only when the emitter's scan sees
// a linear-memory op. Every cell in `store-widths-round-trip.vl` also LOADS, and a
// load already forces the memory — so if the scan forgot the three store names,
// nothing there would notice. Measured: deleting that scan line reddens ZERO corpus
// files without this file, and this file with it. A store instruction in a module
// with no memory section does not validate.
//
// This file exists because the sabotage that should have proven the scan line was
// INERT, and the response to an inert sabotage is to construct its population rather
// than record it as harmless.
function stash(a: i32, v: f64) {
  __store_f64__(a, v)
  0
}
stash(0, 1.5)
stash(8, -2.25)
print(1)
